  "raw_text": "123\n\nKutbi kir briaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto have encircling all around\n \n/ tener rodeando todo alrededor\n\n(Ex/Ej(\ndb-Hibru Nani 12:1\n):\n \nWitnis ailal kutbi kir wan brisa\n \n–\n \nWe have many witnesses encircling all around us\n \n/ Tenemos\nmuchos testigos rodeándonos a nuestro alrededor)\n\nKutbanka\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nwall, fence, enclosure\n \n/ pared, valla, recinto\n\nBila kutbanka\n \n–\n \ninside wall\n \n/ pared interior\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nlfb-63\n):\n \nutla bila kutbanka ra ulbanka ba\n \n–\n \nthe writing on the wall (inside the house)\n \n/ la escritura en la\npared (dentro de la casa))\n\nTaun tnaya kutbanka\n \n(a/t:\n \nTaun naya kutbanka\n,\n \nTaun snaya kutbanka\n) (n/s)\n \n–\n \ncity wall\n \n/ pared de la\ncuidad\n\nKwah\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nfig\n \n/ higo\n\nKwah damni dusa\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nfig tree\n \n/ higuera\n\nKwahadu\n \n(\ndb\n;\n \nCuahado\n-\ndict\n;\n \nKuahado\n-\ndict-alt\n) (n/s)\n \n–\n \ntype of cheese\n \n/ cuajada (queso)\n\nKwahkaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto carry, to transport, to haul, to bring\n \n/ llevar, transportar, traer\n\nDahra kwahkaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto report, to accuse, to gossip, to slander\n \n/ denunciar, acusar, chismear, calumniar\n\n(Lit:\n \nto bring/carry a report/story/accusation\n \n/ traer/llevar un informe/historia/acusación\n)\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nmwb\n-\n09/20\n):\n \nAman kaikpi turi kunin kum dahra kwahkbiara\n \n–\n \nLet’s be careful not to report a false story (false\n\ninformation\n)\n \n/ Tengamos cuidado de no informar una historia falsa (informaci\nó\nn falsa)\n)\n\nDahra kwakwahkra\n \n(n\n-\nagent/s\n-\nagente)\n \n–\n \naccuser\n \n/ acusador\n\n(Note/Nota:\n \nslanderer\n \n/ calumniador\n \n–\n \nNina aisasara\n-\ndb\n,\n \nDahra kwakwahkra\n-\ndb\n,\n \nNina sasauhkra\n-\ndict,lv\n)\n\n(\nEx/Ej\n(\ndb\n-\nParam Marikan\n \n12:10\n):\n \nwan muihni nani dahra kwakwahkra\n \n–\n \naccuser of our\n \nbrothers\n \n/ acusador de\n\nnuestros hermanos\n)\n\nKwâkaia\n \n(Kwakaia)\n \n(\na/t\n:\n \nK\nuakaia\n) (v\n-\ntrans\n; in\ntrans:\n \nKwâwaia\n \n(a/t:\n \nKuawaia\n)\n)\n \n–\n \nto open, to disclose, to uncover\n \n/ abrir,\n\nrevelar, descubrir\n\n(\nEx/Ej\n(\nth\n-\n6\n):\n \nBaibil tikska ba kwâki bri bas tânka kum\n \nmarikisma taim.\n \n–\n \nBe having the Bible text open when you explain.\n \n/ Tenga el\n\ntexto de la Biblia abierto cuando explique.\n)\n\nBîla kwâki langkaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto swallow with an open mouth, to gulp with an open mouth\n \n/ tragar con la boca abierta\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nmwb-12/19)\n:\n \nTasba ba ai bîla kwâki awalka langkan\n \n–\n \nThe earth swallowed up the river\n \n/ La tierra se tragó el río)\n\nDur kwâkaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto open a door\n \n/ abrir una puerta\n\nDur kwâkras\n \n–\n \nclosed door\n \n/ puerta cerrada\n\nKwala\n \n(a/t:\n \nKuala\n) (n/s)\n \n–\n \nclothes, clothing, dress, fabric, ...\n \n/ ropa, vestido, tela,\n \n...\n\n(Construct:\n \nKwailka\n;\n \nKwalkam\n;\n \nKwalka\n)\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nmwb-12/19\n):\n \nlinin kwalka painkira pihni bara klin ba\n \n–\n \nthe fine, white, and clean linen\n \n/ el lino fino, blanco y limpio)\n\nKwala daikaia\n \n(a/t:\n \nKuala daikaia\n) (v)\n \n–\n \nto undress, to take clothes off\n \n/ desnudarse, quitarse la ropa\n\nKwala\n \ndingkaia\n \n(a/t:\n \nKuala dingkaia\n) (v)\n \n–\n \nto dress, to clothe, to put on clothing\n \n/ vestir, vestirse\n\nKwala\n \ndimaia\n \n(a/t:\n \nKuala dimaia\n) (v)\n \n–\n \nto dress oneself, to clothe oneself, to dress, to wear\n \n/ vestirse, ponerse,\nvestir\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nmy102\n):\n \nKwala pihni dimi\n \n–\n \nwearing white clothes\n \n/ vistiendo ropas blancas)\n\nKwala lâkaia\n \n(a/t:\n \nKuala lâkaia\n)\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto dry clothes\n \n/ secar la ropa\n\nKwala lakni\n \n(a/t:\n \nKuala lakni\n)\n \n–\n \nshowy clothes, shiny clothes, flashy clothes /\n \nropa llamativa, ropa brillante\n\nKwala\n \nluha\n \n(a/t:\n \nKuala luha\n)\n \n–\n \nwithout clothes, naked\n \n/ sin ropa, desnuda\n \n(\nSee also/\n \nV\ner también:\n \nSusu\n)\n\nKwala\n \nsipaia\n \n(a/t:\n \nKuala sipaia\n) (v)\n \n–\n \nto sew clothing\n \n/ coser ropa\n\nKwala subaia\n \n(a/t:\n \nKuala subaia\n)\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto wring out clothes\n \n/ exprimir la ropa\n\nKwala\n \ntuskaia\n \n(a\n/t:\n \nKuala tuskaia\n)\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto wash clothes\n \n/ lavar la ropa\n\nKwala\n \ntatuskra\n \n(a/t:\n \nKuala tatuskra\n)\n \n(n\n-\nagent/s\n-\nagente)\n \n–\n \nclothes washer, person who washes\n \nclothes\n \n/\n\nlavador de ropa, persona que lava ropa\n\nKwalhni\n \n(adj)\n \n–\n \nhaving a cavity\n \n/ que tiene cavidad\n\n(Note/Nota: Used as an adjective with\n \nTasba\n, describes terrain that has crevices, cavities, or caves.\n \nNot commonly used.\n \nUntra\n \nis\n\nmore often used.\n \n/ Usado como adjetivo con\n \nTasba\n, describe un terreno que tiene grietas, cavidades o cuevas. No se usa\n\ncomúnmente.\n \nUntra\n \nse usa con más frecuencia.\n)\n\nKwalhwaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto go about being proud\n, to be arrogant, to be haughty\n \n/ andar haciéndose el orgulloso\n, ser arrogante,\n\nser altivo\n\nKwalhwanka\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \narrogance, haughtiness\n \n/ arrogancia\n\nKwamu\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nturkey\n \n/ pavo, chompipe",
